# Programmatically generated De Almeida Qs

section3_en = [{'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'Which island in Western India was the site of the very first fort constructed by Viceroy Almeida in 1505?', 'opts': ['Anjadip Island', 'Diu Island', 'Goa Island', 'Salsette Island'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Almeida began building a fort on Anjadip Island (Angediva) in 1505 to secure the Malabar transit.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': "What is the name of the famous Portuguese fort constructed under Almeida's directives in Cannanore?", 'opts': ['Fort St. Angelo', 'Fort Manuel', 'Fort St. George', 'Fort William'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Fort St. Angelo (Fort de Santo Ângelo) was built in Cannanore in 1505 CE.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'Which fort in Cochin was constructed in alliance with the local Trimumpara Raja to secure the Portuguese base?', 'opts': ['Fort Manuel', 'Fort St. Angelo', 'Fort de Aguada', 'Fort Mormugao'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': "Fort Manuel (Fort Manuel de Kochi) was built in Cochin with the local Raja's permission."}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'Which East African coastal city-state was captured and fortified by Almeida in 1505 before he crossed to India?', 'opts': ['Kilwa', 'Mombasa', 'Zanzibar', 'Mozambique'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Almeida captured and built the Fort of São Tiago at Kilwa to secure the African coast.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'Why did Viceroy Almeida eventually order the demolition of the fort at Anjadip Island?', 'opts': ['It was too difficult to defend and garrison', 'It was destroyed by an earthquake', 'The local ruler paid them to leave', 'He wanted to shift all forces to Malacca'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The fort on Anjadip was vulnerable to local Adil Shahi attacks and hard to supply, leading to its abandonment.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'Which of the following forts were established or occupied by Almeida in 1505? (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['Fort St. Angelo at Cannanore', 'Fort Manuel at Cochin', 'Fort of São Tiago at Kilwa', 'Fort de Diu'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'Cannanore, Cochin, and Kilwa forts were established by Almeida. Diu fort was built much later (1535).'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'What were the strategic functions of Fort St. Angelo in Cannanore? (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['Secure control over the local spice trade of Cannanore', 'Provide a naval base for patrolling the Northern Malabar Coast', 'Blockade the Muslim merchants of Calicut', 'Serve as the official residence of the Mughal Governor'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'Fort St. Angelo secured spice trade, served as a patrol base, and blockaded Calicut. The Mughals had no presence in the region.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'Identify the local rulers who collaborated with Almeida in establishing these fort bases. (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['The Kolathiri Raja of Cannanore', 'The Trimumpara Raja of Cochin', 'The Sultan of Kilwa (vassal ruler)', 'The Sultan of Bijapur'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': "Cannanore's Kolathiri, Cochin's Raja, and Kilwa's vassal ruler cooperated. Bijapur was hostile."}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'What challenges did the Portuguese garrison face in Fort Manuel at Cochin? (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ["Frequent attacks by the Zamorin's forces", 'Shortage of clean drinking water and fresh food', 'Logistical isolation during the monsoon season', 'Invasions by Spanish fleets'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': "Fort Manuel faced Zamorin's attacks, water/food shortages, and monsoon isolation. There were no Spanish attacks."}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'Which construction materials were primarily used to build Fort Manuel in Cochin in 1503-1505? (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['Coconut tree trunks', 'Clay and sand', 'Laterite stone (added later)', 'Italian marble'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'The fort was initially built with coconut trunks and mud, and later reinforced with laterite stone. Marble was not used.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Fort St. Angelo in Cannanore was built on a triangular promontory jutting into the sea.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Its strategic location allowed cannons to cover both the harbor and the land side.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The fort of Kilwa in East Africa was named Fort of São Tiago.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Almeida built it in 1505 to secure the route before crossing the Arabian Sea.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Almeida built a large naval fort at Goa in 1506.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'Goa was captured in 1510 by Albuquerque; Almeida did not fortify Goa.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The local Kolathiri Raja of Cannanore became hostile to the Portuguese during the Siege of Cannanore (1507).', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Local politics and Arab influence led the Raja to besiege the fort in 1507.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Fort Manuel in Cochin was the first European fort constructed in India.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Built in 1503 and reinforced by Almeida in 1505, it was the first European fort on Indian soil.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Almeida personally designed all the architectural layouts of the Cannanore fort.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He commissioned engineers like Tomás Fernandes to design the fortifications.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The fort at Anjadip island was constructed using stone imported directly from Lisbon.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'It was built using local stone and clay found on the island.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The siege of Fort St. Angelo in 1507 was successfully broken by the arrival of a fleet under Tristão da Cunha.', 'ans': True, 'sol': "Tristão da Cunha's fleet arrived with reinforcements, lifting the siege."}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The first European fort constructed in India was Fort __________ in Cochin.', 'ans': 'Manuel', 'sol': 'Fort Manuel de Kochi was built in 1503 CE.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'Viceroy Almeida constructed Fort St. Angelo in the Malabar port city of __________.', 'ans': 'Cannanore', 'sol': "The fort was built to secure Cannanore's harbor."}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'Almeida built a fort on __________ Island to provide a watering station for fleets.', 'ans': 'Anjadip', 'sol': 'Anjadip Island was used as a shelter and repair station.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'In East Africa, Almeida established the Fort of São Tiago at __________.', 'ans': 'Kilwa', 'sol': 'Kilwa was a major trade center on the Swahili Coast.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Portuguese engineer who designed Fort St. Angelo in Cannanore was Tomás __________.', 'ans': 'Fernandes', 'sol': 'Tomas Fernandes was the chief military architect.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The local ruler of Cochin who permitted the construction of Fort Manuel was the __________ Raja.', 'ans': 'Trimumpara', 'sol': 'The Trimumpara Raja (Unni Goda Varma) allied with the Portuguese.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The siege of the Cannanore fort in 1507 was instigated by Arab merchants and the ruler of __________.', 'ans': 'Calicut', 'sol': 'The Zamorin of Calicut coordinated the siege to expel the Portuguese.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The fort at Anjadip was demolished because it was constantly attacked by the forces of the Sultan of __________.', 'ans': 'Bijapur', 'sol': 'The Adil Shahi ruler of Bijapur claimed the island and launched frequent raids.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'Match the Portuguese forts with their locations:', 'items': [{'left': 'Fort Manuel'}, {'left': 'Fort St. Angelo'}, {'left': 'Fort of São Tiago'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'Cochin'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'Cannanore'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'Kilwa'}], 'sol': 'Manuel was in Cochin, St. Angelo in Cannanore, and São Tiago in Kilwa.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'Match the fort bases with their primary strategic reasons for abandonment or defense:', 'items': [{'left': 'Anjadip Fort'}, {'left': 'Cannanore Fort'}, {'left': 'Cochin Fort'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'Demolished due to Adil Shahi attacks'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'Besieged in 1507 by Zamorin coalition'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'Main operational base under Trimumpara alliance'}], 'sol': 'Anjadip was demolished, Cannanore was besieged, and Cochin served as the main allied base.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'Match the fort components with their architectural features:', 'items': [{'left': 'Initial Fort Manuel walls'}, {'left': 'Tomás Fernandes designs'}, {'left': 'Laterite stone reinforcement'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'Built using coconut tree trunks'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'Triangular layout at Cannanore'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'Permanent stone upgrades'}], 'sol': 'Initial walls were coconut trunks, Fernandes designed the triangular layout, and laterite was used for upgrades.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'In what year did the Siege of Cannanore occur?', 'sol': 'Answer: 1507 CE. Explanation: The siege lasted from April to August 1507.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What unique food source saved the Cannanore garrison during the 1507 siege?', 'sol': 'Answer: Crabs washed ashore. Explanation: A sudden wave of crabs provided food when supplies ran out.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Who commanded the garrison during the Siege of Cannanore?', 'sol': 'Answer: Lourenço de Brito. Explanation: Brito was the captain of the fort during the siege.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which sultanate claimed sovereignty over Anjadip Island?', 'sol': 'Answer: The Adil Shahi Sultanate of Bijapur. Explanation: Bijapur launched attacks to reclaim the island.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What name did Almeida give to the fort constructed at Kilwa?', 'sol': 'Answer: Fort of São Tiago. Explanation: It was named after Saint James.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Where did the Portuguese obtain the wood to build Fort Manuel in Cochin?', 'sol': 'Answer: From the local forests provided by the Cochin Raja. Explanation: The Raja supplied timber and labor.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which saint is Fort St. Angelo named after?', 'sol': 'Answer: Saint Angelo. Explanation: The fort was named St. Angelo (Santo Ângelo).'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'How many Portuguese soldiers were left to garrison Anjadip fort initially?', 'sol': 'Answer: Around 80 soldiers. Explanation: A small force was left under Manuel Paçanha.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Almeida demolished the fort at Anjadip island in 1506.\nReason: The fort was difficult to defend against the frequent raids of the Bijapur Sultanate.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Logistical costs and Bijapur raids made Anjadip unsustainable.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Fort Manuel in Cochin was built with the active support of the local Raja.\nReason: The Raja of Cochin sought Portuguese protection against the dominant Zamorin of Calicut.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The alliance was based on mutual interest against Calicut.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Fort St. Angelo was built to dominate the horse trade of Cannanore.\nReason: Cannanore was the chief port for importing Persian horses into the Vijayanagara Empire.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Controlling Cannanore allowed the Portuguese to regulate the lucrative horse trade.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: The Siege of Cannanore in 1507 was led by the British fleet.\nReason: The British wanted to replace the Portuguese as the dominant power on the Malabar Coast.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. The British were not present; the siege was led by the Kolathiri Raja and Calicut.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Almeida built the Fort of São Tiago at Kilwa.\nReason: Kilwa was a strategic Swahili trade center that controlled gold flow from Sofala.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Secure bases in East Africa were critical for the Cape Route navigation.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': "Assertion: The Cannanore garrison survived the 1507 siege because of a sudden supply of crabs.\nReason: A large wave washed thousands of crabs onto the fort's shore, feeding the starving garrison.", 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The event was recorded as a miracle that saved the defenders.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Fort Manuel was built entirely of Portuguese stone brought as ballast.\nReason: There was no local stone suitable for military construction in Cochin.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. The fort was built using local timber/laterite; stone was not imported as ballast for walls.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Almeida prioritized building coastal forts over capturing inland cities.\nReason: Coastal forts supported his Blue Water Policy by securing naval bases for patrols.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Forts were naval support hubs, not centers of territorial administration.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements regarding Fort St. Angelo:\n1. It is located in the city of Cannanore.\n2. It was constructed by Afonso de Albuquerque in 1515.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; it was built by Almeida in 1505.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements about Fort Manuel in Cochin:\n1. It was the first European fort built in India.\n2. The local Raja of Cochin opposed its construction.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; the Raja supported it to gain protection.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to the Kilwa fortification, consider these statements:\n1. Almeida built the Fort of São Tiago there in 1505.\n2. Kilwa is located on the coast of Western India.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; Kilwa is in East Africa.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the statements about Anjadip Island fort:\n1. It was built using local materials in 1505.\n2. It was permanently maintained as the main Portuguese headquarters until 1961.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; the fort was demolished in 1506.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': "With reference to the Siege of Cannanore (1507), consider these statements:\n1. The siege was launched by the Kolathiri Raja supported by the Zamorin.\n2. The garrison was saved by the arrival of Tristão da Cunha's fleet.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?", 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 2, 'sol': 'Both statements are correct. The siege was lifted by reinforcements under Cunha.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did Almeida select Anjadip Island as the site for his first fort?', 'sol': 'Anjadip offered a natural harbor, fresh water, and was located near major shipping lanes, away from hostile mainland rulers.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did the Kolathiri Raja of Cannanore turn against the Portuguese in 1507?', 'sol': 'Arab merchants convinced the Raja that Portuguese naval policies were destroying local trade, and the Portuguese had sunk a ship carrying a Cartaz.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why was Fort Manuel crucial for the survival of the early Portuguese presence in India?', 'sol': 'It protected the Cochin factory and the allied Raja from the superior land forces of the Zamorin of Calicut.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the geographic position of Fort St. Angelo help control Arabian Sea trade?', 'sol': 'It sat on a peninsula, allowing naval guns to command the Cannanore bay and intercept coastal merchant ships.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did Almeida secure the construction of the Kilwa fort in 1505?', 'sol': 'He deposed the hostile Sultan of Kilwa, installed a cooperative vassal, and constructed Fort São Tiago using local labor.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the Portuguese reinforce Fort Manuel over the years?', 'sol': 'They replaced the original coconut log palisade with a permanent laterite stone structure and added heavy artillery bastions.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Analyze the logistical issues that led to the abandonment and demolition of Anjadip Fort.', 'sol': 'The island was isolated during monsoons, faced continuous attacks from Bijapur forces, and was too expensive to garrison without commercial benefits.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Examine the role of local alliances in the fortification strategy of Francisco de Almeida.', 'sol': 'Almeida relied on rivalries (like Cochin vs. Calicut) to secure land for forts, showing that local divisions facilitated European entry.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Discuss the military significance of the Siege of Cannanore (1507) for Portuguese naval tactics.', 'sol': 'The siege demonstrated that coastal forts could withstand massive land blockades if they were periodically resupplied by sea.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': "Explain the concept of 'feitoria' fortification.", 'sol': 'It is the process of enclosing a commercial factory/warehouse with walls and bastions to protect trade goods from local riots or attacks.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Describe the design features of Fort St. Angelo in Cannanore.', 'sol': 'Designed by Tomás Fernandes, it had a triangular layout, stone battlements, and gun positions facing both the harbor and land approaches.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain why the Portuguese prioritized building coastal and island forts rather than inland networks.', 'sol': 'Portugal had a small population, so they relied on naval mobility; coastal forts acted as bases for ships, which was their main strength.'}]

section3_hi = [{'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'पश्चिमी भारत का कौन सा द्वीप 1505 में वायसराय अल्मेडा द्वारा निर्मित सबसे पहले किले का स्थल था?', 'opts': ['अंजादीप द्वीप', 'दीव द्वीप', 'गोवा द्वीप', 'सालसेट द्वीप'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'अल्मेडा ने मालाबार पारगमन को सुरक्षित करने के लिए 1505 में अंजादीप द्वीप (अंगेदिवा) पर एक किला बनाना शुरू किया।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'कन्नूर में अल्मेडा के निर्देशों के तहत निर्मित प्रसिद्ध पुर्तगाली किले का क्या नाम है?', 'opts': ['फोर्ट सेंट एंजेलो', 'फोर्ट मैनुअल', 'फोर्ट सेंट जॉर्ज', 'फोर्ट विलियम'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'फोर्ट सेंट एंजेलो (कन्नूर) का निर्माण 1505 ईस्वी में हुआ था।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'पुर्तगाली आधार को सुरक्षित करने के लिए स्थानीय त्रिमुम्पारा राजा के साथ गठबंधन में कोचीन में किस किले का निर्माण किया गया था?', 'opts': ['फोर्ट मैनुअल', 'फोर्ट सेंट एंजेलो', 'फोर्ट डी अगुआडा', 'फोर्ट मर्मगाओ'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'फोर्ट मैनुअल (कोचीन) का निर्माण स्थानीय राजा की अनुमति से पुर्तगाली आधार के रूप में किया गया था।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'भारत जाने से पहले 1505 में अल्मेडा द्वारा किस पूर्वी अफ्रीकी तटीय शहर-राज्य पर कब्जा कर लिया गया था और वहां किलेबंदी की गई थी?', 'opts': ['किलवा', 'मोम्बासा', 'जंजीबार', 'मोजाम्बिक'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'अल्मेडा ने अफ्रीकी तट को सुरक्षित करने के लिए किलवा में सूबा (São Tiago) का किला बनाया।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'वायसराय अल्मेडा ने अंततः अंजादीप द्वीप के किले को ध्वस्त करने का आदेश क्यों दिया?', 'opts': ['इसकी रक्षा करना और सैनिकों को रखना बहुत कठिन था', 'यह भूकंप से नष्ट हो गया था', 'स्थानीय शासक ने उन्हें जाने के लिए भुगतान किया था', 'वह सभी बलों को मलक्का स्थानांतरित करना चाहते थे'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'अंजादीप का किला स्थानीय आदिल शाही हमलों के प्रति संवेदनशील था और इसकी आपूर्ति कठिन थी, जिससे इसे छोड़ना पड़ा।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': '1505 में अल्मेडा द्वारा निम्नलिखित में से कौन से किले स्थापित या अधिकृत किए गए थे? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['कन्नूर में फोर्ट सेंट एंजेलो', 'कोचीन में फोर्ट मैनुअल', 'किलवा में साओ टियागो का किला', 'दीव का किला'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'कन्नूर, कोचीन और किलवा किलों की स्थापना अल्मेडा ने की थी। दीव का किला बाद में (1535) बना।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'कन्नूर में फोर्ट सेंट एंजेलो के रणनीतिक कार्य क्या थे? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['कन्नूर के स्थानीय मसाला व्यापार पर सुरक्षित नियंत्रण', 'उत्तरी मालाबार तट पर गश्त के लिए एक नौसैनिक अड्डा प्रदान करना', 'कालीकट के मुस्लिम व्यापारियों की नाकेबंदी करना', 'मुगल गवर्नर के आधिकारिक निवास के रूप में सेवा करना'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'इस किले ने मसाला व्यापार को सुरक्षित किया, गश्ती अड्डे के रूप में कार्य किया, और कालीकट की नाकेबंदी की।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'इन किला अड्डों को स्थापित करने में अल्मेडा के साथ सहयोग करने वाले स्थानीय शासकों की पहचान करें। (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['कन्नूर के कोलाथिरी राजा', 'कोचीन के त्रिमुम्पारा राजा', 'किलवा के सुल्तान (जागीरदार शासक)', 'बीजापुर के सुल्तान'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'कन्नूर के कोलाथिरी, कोचीन के राजा और किलवा के जागीरदार ने सहयोग किया। बीजापुर शत्रुतापूर्ण था।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'कोचीन के फोर्ट मैनुअल में पुर्तगाली सेना को किन चुनौतियों का सामना करना पड़ा? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['ज़मोरिन की सेनाओं द्वारा बार-बार हमले', 'साफ पीने के पानी और ताजे भोजन की कमी', 'मानसून के मौसम के दौरान रसद अलगाव', 'स्पेनिश बेड़े द्वारा आक्रमण'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'फोर्ट मैनुअल को ज़मोरिन के हमलों, पानी/भोजन की कमी और मानसून में अलगाव का सामना करना पड़ा।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': '1503-1505 में कोचीन में फोर्ट मैनुअल बनाने के लिए मुख्य रूप से किस निर्माण सामग्री का उपयोग किया गया था? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['नारियल के पेड़ के तने', 'मिट्टी और रेत', 'लैटेराइट पत्थर (बाद में जोड़ा गया)', 'इतालवी संगमरमर'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'किले का निर्माण शुरू में नारियल के तनों और मिट्टी से किया गया था, और बाद में इसे लैटेराइट पत्थर से मजबूत किया गया।'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'फोर्ट सेंट एंजेलो in Cannanore was built on a triangular promontory jutting into the sea.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Its strategic location allowed cannons to cover both the harbor and the land side.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The fort of Kilwa in East Africa was named Fort of São Tiago.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'अल्मेडा built it in 1505 to secure the route before crossing the Arabian Sea.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'अल्मेडा built a large naval fort at Goa in 1506.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'Goa was captured in 1510 by Albuquerque; अल्मेडा did not fortify Goa.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The local Kolathiri Raja of Cannanore became hostile to the Portuguese during the Siege of Cannanore (1507).', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Local politics and Arab influence led the Raja to besiege the fort in 1507.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'फोर्ट मैनुअल in Cochin was the first European fort constructed in India.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Built in 1503 and reinforced by अल्मेडा in 1505, it was the first European fort on Indian soil.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'अल्मेडा personally designed all the architectural layouts of the Cannanore fort.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He commissioned engineers like Tomás Fernandes to design the fortifications.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The fort at Anjadip island was constructed using stone imported directly from Lisbon.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'It was built using local stone and clay found on the island.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The siege of फोर्ट सेंट एंजेलो in 1507 was successfully broken by the arrival of a fleet under Tristão da Cunha.', 'ans': True, 'sol': "Tristão da Cunha's fleet arrived with reinforcements, lifting the siege."}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The first European fort constructed in India was Fort __________ in Cochin.', 'ans': 'Manuel', 'sol': 'Fort Manuel de Kochi was built in 1503 CE.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'Viceroy अल्मेडा constructed Fort St. Angelo in the Malabar port city of __________.', 'ans': 'Cannanore', 'sol': "The fort was built to secure Cannanore's harbor."}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'अल्मेडा built a fort on __________ Island to provide a watering station for fleets.', 'ans': 'Anjadip', 'sol': 'Anjadip Island was used as a shelter and repair station.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'In East Africa, अल्मेडा established the Fort of São Tiago at __________.', 'ans': 'Kilwa', 'sol': 'Kilwa was a major trade center on the Swahili Coast.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Portuguese engineer who designed Fort St. Angelo in कन्नूर was Tomás __________.', 'ans': 'Fernandes', 'sol': 'Tomas Fernandes was the chief military architect.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The local ruler of Cochin who permitted the construction of Fort Manuel was the __________ Raja.', 'ans': 'Trimumpara', 'sol': 'The Trimumpara Raja (Unni Goda Varma) allied with the Portuguese.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The siege of the कन्नूर fort in 1507 was instigated by Arab merchants and the ruler of __________.', 'ans': 'Calicut', 'sol': 'The Zamorin of Calicut coordinated the siege to expel the Portuguese.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The fort at Anjadip was demolished because it was constantly attacked by the forces of the Sultan of __________.', 'ans': 'Bijapur', 'sol': 'The Adil Shahi ruler of Bijapur claimed the island and launched frequent raids.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'पुर्तगाली किलों का उनके स्थानों से मिलान करें:', 'items': [{'left': 'फोर्ट मैनुअल'}, {'left': 'फोर्ट सेंट एंजेलो'}, {'left': 'फोर्ट ऑफ साओ टियागो'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'कोचीन'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'कन्नूर'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'किलवा'}], 'sol': 'मैनुअल कोचीन में, सेंट एंजेलो कन्नूर में, और साओ टियागो किलवा में था।'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'किला अड्डों का उनके परित्याग या रक्षा के प्राथमिक रणनीतिक कारणों से मिलान करें:', 'items': [{'left': 'अंजादीप किला'}, {'left': 'कन्नूर किला'}, {'left': 'कोचीन किला'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'आदिल शाही हमलों के कारण ध्वस्त कर दिया गया'}, {'val': '1', 'text': '1507 में ज़मोरिन गठबंधन द्वारा घेराबंदी की गई'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'त्रिमुम्पारा गठबंधन के तहत मुख्य परिचालन आधार'}], 'sol': 'अंजादीप को ध्वस्त कर दिया गया, कन्नूर को घेर लिया गया, और कोचीन मुख्य सहयोगी आधार के रूप में कार्य करता था।'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'किले के घटकों का उनकी स्थापत्य विशेषताओं से मिलान करें:', 'items': [{'left': 'प्रारंभिक फोर्ट मैनुअल दीवारें'}, {'left': 'टॉमास फर्नांडीस डिजाइन'}, {'left': 'लैटेराइट पत्थर सुदृढ़ीकरण'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'नारियल के पेड़ के तनों का उपयोग करके निर्मित'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'कन्नूर में त्रिकोणीय लेआउट'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'स्थायी पत्थर उन्नयन'}], 'sol': 'प्रारंभिक दीवारें नारियल के तने थे, फर्नांडीस ने त्रिकोणीय लेआउट डिजाइन किया, और बाद में लैटेराइट का उपयोग किया गया।'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'In what year did the Siege of कन्नूर occur?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: 1507 CE.। स्पष्टीकरण: The siege lasted from April to August 1507.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What unique food source saved the कन्नूर garrison during the 1507 siege?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: Crabs washed ashore.। स्पष्टीकरण: A sudden wave of crabs provided food when supplies ran out.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Who commanded the garrison during the Siege of कन्नूर?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: Lourenço de Brito.। स्पष्टीकरण: Brito was the captain of the fort during the siege.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which sultanate claimed sovereignty over Anjadip Island?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: The Adil Shahi Sultanate of Bijapur.। स्पष्टीकरण: Bijapur launched attacks to reclaim the island.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What name did अल्मेडा give to the fort constructed at Kilwa?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: Fort of São Tiago.। स्पष्टीकरण: It was named after Saint James.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Where did the Portuguese obtain the wood to build फोर्ट मैनुअल in Cochin?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: From the local forests provided by the Cochin Raja.। स्पष्टीकरण: The Raja supplied timber and labor.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which saint is Fort St. Angelo named after?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: Saint Angelo.। स्पष्टीकरण: The fort was named St. Angelo (Santo Ângelo).'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'How many Portuguese soldiers were left to garrison Anjadip fort initially?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: Around 80 soldiers.। स्पष्टीकरण: A small force was left under Manuel Paçanha.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: अल्मेडा demolished the fort at Anjadip island in 1506.\nकारण: The fort was difficult to defend against the frequent raids of the Bijapur Sultanate.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Logistical costs and Bijapur raids made Anjadip unsustainable.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: Fort Manuel in Cochin was built with the active support of the local Raja.\nकारण: The Raja of Cochin sought Portuguese protection against the dominant Zamorin of Calicut.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The alliance was based on mutual interest against Calicut.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: Fort St. Angelo was built to dominate the horse trade of Cannanore.\nकारण: Cannanore was the chief port for importing Persian horses into the Vijayanagara Empire.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Controlling Cannanore allowed the Portuguese to regulate the lucrative horse trade.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: The Siege of Cannanore in 1507 was led by the British fleet.\nकारण: The British wanted to replace the Portuguese as the dominant power on the Malabar Coast.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. The British were not present; the siege was led by the Kolathiri Raja and Calicut.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: अल्मेडा built the Fort of São Tiago at Kilwa.\nकारण: Kilwa was a strategic Swahili trade center that controlled gold flow from Sofala.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Secure bases in East Africa were critical for the Cape Route navigation.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': "अभिकथन: The Cannanore garrison survived the 1507 siege because of a sudden supply of crabs.\nकारण: A large wave washed thousands of crabs onto the fort's shore, feeding the starving garrison.", 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The event was recorded as a miracle that saved the defenders.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: Fort Manuel was built entirely of Portuguese stone brought as ballast.\nकारण: There was no local stone suitable for military construction in Cochin.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. The fort was built using local timber/laterite; stone was not imported as ballast for walls.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: अल्मेडा prioritized building coastal forts over capturing inland cities.\nकारण: Coastal forts supported his Blue Water Policy by securing naval bases for patrols.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Forts were naval support hubs, not centers of territorial administration.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements regarding Fort St. Angelo:\n1. It is located in the city of कन्नूर.\n2. It was constructed by Afonso de Albuquerque in 1515.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; it was built by अल्मेडा in 1505.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements about फोर्ट मैनुअल in Cochin:\n1. It was the first European fort built in India.\n2. The local Raja of Cochin opposed its construction.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; the Raja supported it to gain protection.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to the Kilwa fortification, consider these statements:\n1. अल्मेडा built the Fort of São Tiago there in 1505.\n2. Kilwa is located on the coast of Western India.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; Kilwa is in East Africa.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the statements about Anjadip Island fort:\n1. It was built using local materials in 1505.\n2. It was permanently maintained as the main Portuguese headquarters until 1961.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; the fort was demolished in 1506.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': "With reference to the Siege of कन्नूर (1507), consider these statements:\n1. The siege was launched by the Kolathiri Raja supported by the Zamorin.\n2. The garrison was saved by the arrival of Tristão da Cunha's fleet.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?", 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 2, 'sol': 'Both statements are correct. The siege was lifted by reinforcements under Cunha.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did अल्मेडा select Anjadip Island as the site for his first fort?', 'sol': 'Anjadip offered a natural harbor, fresh water, and was located near major shipping lanes, away from hostile mainland rulers.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did the Kolathiri Raja of कन्नूर turn against the Portuguese in 1507?', 'sol': 'Arab merchants convinced the Raja that Portuguese naval policies were destroying local trade, and the Portuguese had sunk a ship carrying a Cartaz.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why was फोर्ट मैनुअल crucial for the survival of the early Portuguese presence in India?', 'sol': 'It protected the Cochin factory and the allied Raja from the superior land forces of the Zamorin of Calicut.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the geographic position of Fort St. Angelo help control Arabian Sea trade?', 'sol': 'It sat on a peninsula, allowing naval guns to command the Cannanore bay and intercept coastal merchant ships.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did अल्मेडा secure the construction of the Kilwa fort in 1505?', 'sol': 'He deposed the hostile Sultan of Kilwa, installed a cooperative vassal, and constructed Fort São Tiago using local labor.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the Portuguese reinforce फोर्ट मैनुअल over the years?', 'sol': 'They replaced the original coconut log palisade with a permanent laterite stone structure and added heavy artillery bastions.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Analyze the logistical issues that led to the abandonment and demolition of Anjadip Fort.', 'sol': 'The island was isolated during monsoons, faced continuous attacks from Bijapur forces, and was too expensive to garrison without commercial benefits.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Examine the role of local alliances in the fortification strategy of Francisco de अल्मेडा.', 'sol': 'अल्मेडा relied on rivalries (like Cochin vs. Calicut) to secure land for forts, showing that local divisions facilitated European entry.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Discuss the military significance of the Siege of कन्नूर (1507) for Portuguese naval tactics.', 'sol': 'The siege demonstrated that coastal forts could withstand massive land blockades if they were periodically resupplied by sea.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': "Explain the concept of 'feitoria' fortification.", 'sol': 'It is the process of enclosing a commercial factory/warehouse with walls and bastions to protect trade goods from local riots or attacks.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Describe the design features of Fort St. Angelo in कन्नूर.', 'sol': 'Designed by Tomás Fernandes, it had a triangular layout, stone battlements, and gun positions facing both the harbor and land approaches.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain why the Portuguese prioritized building coastal and island forts rather than inland networks.', 'sol': 'Portugal had a small population, so they relied on naval mobility; coastal forts acted as bases for ships, which was their main strength.'}]
